hority SHALL leave these tools\\nunavailable rather than silently substituting a hosted or Sandbox path.\",\n    \"The three tools SHALL be advertised when the process has accepted native\\nhost authority or has a configured Knowledge root; an absolute path on a\\nprocess without accepted native authority SHALL fail closed with\\n`executor_unavailable` rather than resolving through a hosted, Knowledge, or\\nSandbox path.\",\n)\nr_auth = sub(\n    r_auth,\n    \"A Run\\nSHALL bind to the trusted native executor identity on its first native\\noperation, including `read`, and SHALL remain bound to it;\",\n    \"A Run\\nSHALL bind to the trusted native executor identity on its first absolute-path\\noperation, including `read`, and SHALL remain bound to it; a `kb://` operation\\nSHALL NOT bind or require an executor identity;\",\n)\nr_auth = sub(\n    r_auth,\n    \"- **AND** the result identifies the absolute path and does not invent a Knowledge Space binding\\n\",\n    \"- **AND** the result identifies the absolute path and does not invent a Knowledge Space binding\\n\\n#### Scenario: Absolute path without accepted native authority fails closed\\n\\n- **WHEN** the process has a configured Knowledge root and no `tools.nativeExecutorId`, and the model calls `read` with an absolute path\\n- **THEN** the tool returns `executor_unavailable`\\n- **AND** it does not resolve the path through the Knowledge root or any other authority\\n\",\n)\n\nr_sel = block(dl, \"Read selectors and context are deterministic\")\nr_sel = sub(\n    r_sel,\n    \"A valid selector SHALL be normalized once to the\\ninternal zero-based range. Existing literal paths SHALL take precedence over\\nselector parsing.\",\n    \"A valid selector SHALL be normalized once to the\\ninternal zero-based range. The tool SHALL recognize a `scheme://` prefix before\\nsplitting a trailing selector, so a scheme's own colon is never read as a\\nselector. For absolute paths, existing literal paths SHALL take precedence over\\nselector parsing; a `kb://` path component SHALL NOT contain `:`, so the split is\\nunambiguous without probing. A `path` that begins with a `scheme://` prefix the\\ntool does not implement SHALL fail closed with `invalid_path` on every tool and\\nSHALL NOT be treated as a relative or literal filename.\",\n)\nr_sel = sub(\n    r_sel,\n    \"#### Scenario: Directory range has no context lines\\n\",\n    \"#### Scenario: Unknown scheme fails closed\\n\\n- **WHEN** the model calls `read`, `edit`, or `write` with a path such as `vault://notes/a.md`\\n- **THEN** the tool returns `invalid_path`\\n- **AND** no file named `vault:` or `vault://notes/a.md` is read, created, or modified\\n\\n#### Scenario: Directory range has no context lines\\n\",\n)\n\nr_write = block(nft, \"Write creates only\")\nr_write = sub(\n    r_write,\n    \"`write` SHALL create a new regular file when the absolute target is absent. It\\nSHALL fail with `file_exists` when the target already exists, regardless of the\\nprovided content.\",\n    \"`write` SHALL create a new regular file when the target is absent, creating\\nmissing intermediate directories beneath the resolved authority root on every\\nscheme. It SHALL fail with `file_exists` when the target already exists,\\nregardless of the provided content, and with `not_regular_file` when an\\nintermediate path component exists and is not a directory.\",\n)\nr_write = sub(\n    r_write,\n    \"#### Scenario: Existing file is protected\\n\",\n    \"#### Scenario: Missing intermediate directories are created\\n\\n- **WHEN** write targets `research/2026/note.md` beneath a root where `research/` does not exist\\n- **THEN** the intermediate directories and the file are created\\n- **AND** an intermediate component that exists as a regular file fails with `not_regular_file` and creates nothing\\n\\n#### Scenario: Existing file is protected\\n\",\n)\n\nr_fence = block(nft, \"Native mutations have a durable pre-effect fence\")\nr_fence = sub(\n    r_fence,\n    \"Before an alpha native `edit` or `write` changes bytes, the trusted runtime SHALL\\ndurably record a stable mutation attempt identity and target operation metadata.\",\n    \"Before an alpha native `edit` or `write` changes bytes on any scheme, the\\ntrusted runtime SHALL durably record a stable mutation attempt identity and\\ntarget operation metadata. The recorded target for a `kb://` mutation SHALL be\\nthe locator, never the resolved host path. Executor binding is an absolute-path\\nconcern; a `kb://` attempt SHALL be fenced and replayed without binding the Run\\nto a worker.\",\n)\nr_fence = sub(\n    r_fence,\n    \"#### Scenario: Settled native mutation replays safely\\n\",\n    \"#### Scenario: Knowledge mutation is fenced on any worker\\n\\n- **WHEN** a worker dies after recording a `kb://` edit attempt and a different worker retries the Run\\n- **THEN** recovery reports `outcome_unknown` on that worker\\n- **AND** the retry does not execute the edit again and does not fail with `executor_unavailable`\\n\\n#### Scenario: Settled native mutation replays safely\\n\",\n)\n\nr_kb = \"\"\"### Requirement: Knowledge locators resolve through trusted owner authority\n\n`read`, `edit`, and `write` SHALL accept `kb://<space-id>/<path>[:selector]`,\nwhere `<space-id>` is the stable Knowledge Space identifier and `<path>` is a\nKnowledge-relative path. The tool SHALL resolve the identifier through the\ntrusted Run owner's current access immediately before opening the child, under\ntenant enforcement, on every call. An absent, removed, malformed, or other-owner\nidentifier SHALL return the same closed `knowledge_space_not_found` result. A\ncurrently owned Space whose root or stable-ID child cannot be resolved safely\nSHALL return `knowledge_space_unavailable`. Neither result SHALL reveal whether\nanother owner, row, or directory exists, and the tool SHALL NOT probe candidate\ndirectories.\n\nPath validation SHALL reject absolute paths, empty components, `.` or `..`\ncomponents, backslashes, `:`, NUL or control characters, and paths above 1,024\nUTF-8 bytes or 32 components, returning `invalid_path`. It SHALL refuse every\nsymbolic-link component or entry without following it, returning `not_found`.\n`kb://<space-id>` and `kb://<space-id>/` SHALL address the Space's directory and\nlist it under the directory listing requirements; a bare `kb://` or a locator\nwith no identifier SHALL fail with `invalid_path`. Beyond those rules, `kb://`\ntargets SHALL follow the same regular-file, directory, selector, context,\ntruncation, mutation, and `file_exists` behavior as absolute paths. No\nMarkdown-only or per-file byte policy SHALL apply to `kb://` operations.\n\nEvery `kb://` result SHALL identify the target by its locator and SHALL carry\nthe response-time Knowledge Space identifier and display name. It SHALL expose\nno configured root, resolved child path, hosted owner ID, credential, worker\nidentity, or raw filesystem diagnostic. Every successful `kb://` read or listing\nSHALL include the Knowledge untrusted-content `notice`; content SHALL be returned\nverbatim so that `edit` `oldText` can be copied from it.\n\nThe `kb://` grammar is the authority-aware locator that later schemes follow; a\nscheme SHALL declare which of `read`, `edit`, and `write` it supports, and an\nunsupported operation SHALL return a structured error without side effects.\n\n#### Scenario: Search locator opens the passage\n\n- **WHEN** the model calls `read` with a locator returned by `knowledge_search`, such as `kb://<id>/research/note.md:41-53`\n- **THEN** the tool returns lines 41 through 53 with one adjacent context line on each side, numbered as native reads number them\n- **AND** the result carries the Space identifier, display name, locator, and untrusted-content notice\n\n#### Scenario: Another owner's Space is unresolvable\n\n- **WHEN** the model supplies a locator whose identifier belongs to another owner\n- **THEN** the tool returns `knowledge_space_not_found`\n- **AND** the result is identical to the result for an absent identifier and no file is opened\n\n#### Scenario: Locator carries no host authority\n\n- **WHEN** a `kb://` read, edit, or write executes on a worker with no `tools.nativeExecutorId`\n- **THEN** it resolves through the worker's configured Knowledge root and the Run owner\n- **AND** it does not require or record an executor binding\n\n#### Scenario: Space directory is listed\n\n- **WHEN** the model calls `read` with `kb://<id>/`\n- **THEN** the result is the deterministic two-level listing of the Space's directory with every entry shown as native listings show it\n- **AND** the header is the locator as given\n\n#### Scenario: Non-Markdown file is readable and writable\n\n- **WHEN** the model writes `kb://<id>/data/table.csv` and then reads it back\n- **THEN** both operations succeed under ordinary native semantics\n- **AND** no Markdown-suffix or 1 MiB rule rejects either call\n\n#### Scenario: Colon inside a Knowledge path is rejected\n\n- **WHEN** the model calls `read` with `kb://<id>/notes/a:b.md`\n- **THEN** the tool returns `invalid_path`\n- **AND** it does not interpret `b.md` as a selector or probe for a literal file\n\n#### Scenario: Edit copies verbatim content\n\n- **WHEN** a note contains `<system>` in its text and the model reads it through `kb://` and then edits it using that text as `oldText`\n- **THEN** the read returned the text unchanged\n- **AND** the edit finds exactly one match and applies\n\"\"\"\n\nnative_delta = f\"\"\"## MODIFIED Requirements\n\n{r_auth}\n{r_sel}\n{r_write}\n{r_fence}\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n{r_kb}\n## REMOVED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: Knowledge read reuses the native reader and is deprecated\n\n**Reason**: `knowledge_read` is deleted. `read` with a `kb://` locator carries\nthe owner and Space authorization the adapter existed to preserve, and the\nlegacy envelope, Markdown-only rule, and 1 MiB source policy have no replacement.\n\n**Migration**: Call `read` with the `kb://<space-id>/<path>[:selector]` locator\nreturned by `knowledge_search`. Remove `knowledge_read` from `tools.allowed`;\nboot validation rejects the unknown id. Historical `knowledge_read` observations\nrender as recorded; a Run whose immutable tool snapshot names `knowledge_read`\nfails that call closed as unavailable.\n\"\"\"\nwrite(\"native-file-tools/spec.md\", native_delta)\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- knowledge-tools\nkt = (SPECS / \"knowledge-tools/spec.md\").read_text()\n\nk_auth = block(kt, \"Knowledge tools derive filesystem authority only from trusted Run context\")\nk_auth = sub(\n    k_auth,\n    \"The system SHALL register `knowledge_search` and `knowledge_read` as code-owned `read_only` tools. Their executors SHALL receive\",\n    \"The system SHALL register `knowledge_search` as a code-owned `read_only` tool; Knowledge file reads, edits, and writes are the `kb://` locator of the native file tools. Its executor SHALL receive\",\n)\nk_auth = sub(\n    k_auth,\n    \"At Run acceptance, Knowledge tool eligibility SHALL depend on\",\n    \"At Run acceptance, `knowledge_search` eligibility SHALL depend on\",\n)\nk_auth = sub(\n    k_auth,\n    \"an otherwise-eligible Knowledge tool SHALL remain advertised when the owner currently has zero spaces; a later call SHALL signal `knowledge_space_not_configured` to the model. When `knowledge.root` is absent from the authoring API process, the existing closed `knowledge_space_unavailable` manifest state SHALL apply without probing the filesystem on the request path.\",\n    \"an otherwise-eligible `knowledge_search` SHALL remain advertised when the owner currently has zero spaces; a later call SHALL signal `knowledge_space_not_configured` to the model. When `knowledge.root` is absent from the authoring API process, the existing closed `knowledge_space_unavailable` manifest state SHALL apply without probing the filesystem on the request path. The same configured root SHALL make the native `read`, `edit`, and `write` tools eligible for `kb://` locators as defined by `native-file-tools`.\",\n)\n\nk_search = block(kt, \"Knowledge search scans one or all current spaces deterministically within global bounds\")\nk_search = sub(\n    k_search,\n    \"Every returned passage SHALL carry the response-time Knowledge Space identifier and display name, exact Knowledge-relative path, zero-based `offset`, source-line `limit` from 1 through 2,000, and an `excerpt` of at most 500 Unicode code points. `offset` and `limit` SHALL identify the complete emitted source-line window and be directly valid `knowledge_read` arguments for that file. If the window exceeds the excerpt cap, search SHALL crop visibly around a literal match without changing the source-line coordinates. Search SHALL NOT duplicate a separate matching-line string, expose a match mode while only literal search exists, or expose a content hash or revision token.\",\n    \"Every returned passage SHALL carry the response-time Knowledge Space identifier and display name, exact Knowledge-relative path, a `locator` of the form `kb://<space-id>/<path>:<start>-<end>` whose one-based inclusive line range is the complete emitted source-line window and which is directly a valid `read` argument, and an `excerpt` of at most 500 Unicode code points. A passage SHALL span at most 2,000 logical lines. Search SHALL NOT emit zero-based coordinates. If the window exceeds the excerpt cap, search SHALL crop visibly around a literal match without changing the locator's range. Search SHALL NOT duplicate a separate matching-line string, expose a match mode while only literal search exists, or expose a content hash or revision token.\",\n)\nk_search = sub(\n    k_search,\n    \"- **AND** every matching line remains covered in deterministic offset order by coordinates accepted by `knowledge_read`\",\n    \"- **AND** every matching line remains covered in deterministic order by locators accepted by `read`\",\n)\nk_search = sub(\n    k_search,\n    \"#### Scenario: Search passage expands through read\\n\\n- **WHEN** an assistant passes a search result's space ID, path, offset, and limit to `knowledge_read`\\n- **THEN** read addresses the complete current logical-line window represented by those coordinates\\n- **AND** neither call requires a model-facing file hash\",\n    \"#### Scenario: Search passage expands through read\\n\\n- **WHEN** an assistant passes a search result's `locator` unchanged to `read`\\n- **THEN** read addresses the complete current logical-line window the passage covered, plus native context lines\\n- **AND** neither call requires a model-facing file hash or a second coordinate system\",\n)\nk_search = sub(\n    k_search,\n    \"- **AND** each result carries reusable zero-based line coordinates and a bounded excerpt without a content hash\",\n    \"- **AND** each result carries a reusable `kb://` locator and a bounded excerpt without a content hash\",\n)\nk_search = sub(\n    k_search,\n    \"Search SHALL return passages in deterministic space `(createdAt, id)`, relative-path, and zero-based passage-offset order.\",\n    \"Search SHALL return passages in deterministic space `(createdAt, id)`, relative-path, and passage start-line order.\",\n)\n\nk_attr = block(kt, \"Retrieval persists safe response-time attribution\")\nk_attr = sub(\n    k_attr,\n    \"Every newly successful search passage and read result SHALL include the logical Knowledge Space identifier, response-time display name, exact Knowledge-relative path, and zero-based line coordinates. Search SHALL additionally include its bounded excerpt; read SHALL include returned Markdown and optional continuation.\",\n    \"Every newly successful search passage SHALL include the logical Knowledge Space identifier, response-time display name, exact Knowledge-relative path, `kb://` locator with its one-based line range, and bounded excerpt. `kb://` read, listing, edit, and write results follow the native file tools' result contract and carry the same Space identifier and display name.\",\n)\nk_attr = sub(\n    k_attr,\n    \"- **WHEN** a Chat uses a newly successful Knowledge passage or ranged read and the browser reloads\\n- **THEN** the reconstructed result retains the same space identifier, response-time name, path, coordinates, and recorded excerpt or content\",\n    \"- **WHEN** a Chat uses a newly successful Knowledge passage and the browser reloads\\n- **THEN** the reconstructed result retains the same space identifier, response-time name, path, locator, and recorded excerpt\",\n)\nk_attr = sub(\n    k_attr,\n    \"- **THEN** the persisted result retains its original response-time name, path, coordinates, excerpt, or content\\n- **AND** a later tool call may return different metadata, coordinates, or bytes\",\n    \"- **THEN** the persisted result retains its original response-time name, path, locator, and excerpt\\n- **AND** a later tool call may return different metadata, ranges, or bytes\",\n)\nk_attr = sub(\n    k_attr,\n    \"Calls authored before this change remain executable because the new read range and search cursor arguments are optional.\",\n    \"Historical `knowledge_read` observations SHALL render as recorded; the tool itself no longer exists and a Run whose snapshot names it fails that call closed as unavailable.\",\n)\n\nk_trust = block(kt, \"Knowledge content is untrusted and potentially stale\")\nk_trust = sub(\n    k_trust,\n    \"Knowledge tool declarations and model-visible results SHALL identify filesystem content as owner-maintained, untrusted context that may be stale.\",\n    \"The `knowledge_search` declaration, the native `read` declaration's `kb://` guidance, and every model-visible Knowledge result, including `kb://` reads and listings, SHALL identify filesystem content as owner-maintained, untrusted context that may be stale through the closed notice. `kb://` content SHALL NOT be rewritten or neutralized by the runtime; the framing is carried by the notice and the declarations so that returned bytes remain usable as exact `edit` targets.\",\n)\nk_trust = sub(\n    k_trust,\n    \"#### Scenario: Note contains a volatile claim\\n\",\n    \"#### Scenario: Knowledge read carries the notice verbatim\\n\\n- **WHEN** the model reads a note through `kb://`\\n- **THEN** the result includes the closed untrusted-content notice\\n- **AND** the note's text is returned byte-for-byte within the selected range\\n\\n#### Scenario: Note contains a volatile claim\\n\",\n)\n\nk_read_removed = \"\"\"### Requirement: Knowledge read returns one explicitly selected safe live Markdown range\n\n**Reason**: Replaced by `read` with a `kb://<space-id>/<path>[:selector]`\nlocator, which keeps the owner/Space authorization, path validation, and\nsymbolic-link refusal while dropping the Knowledge-specific envelope, zero-based\ncoordinates, Markdown-only suffix rule, and 1 MiB source policy.\n\n**Migration**: Use the `locator` field of each `knowledge_search` passage as the\n`read` argument, or compose `kb://<space-id>/<path>` from a known Space and\npath. Remove `knowledge_read` from `tools.allowed`.\n\"\"\"\n\nkt_delta = f\"\"\"## MODIFIED Requirements\n\n{k_auth}\n{k_search}\n{k_attr}\n{k_trust}\n## REMOVED Requirements\n\n{k_read_removed}\"\"\"\nwrite(\"knowledge-tools/spec.md\", kt_delta)\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- tool-calling\ntc = (SPECS / \"tool-calling/spec.md\").read_text()\n\nt_reg = block(tc, \"Tool registry with mandatory safety classification\")\nt_reg = sub(\n    t_reg,\n    \"Alpha-native tools carry explicit host authority; they are not a\\ngeneral permission engine or a remote MCP write grant.\",\n    \"Alpha-native tools carry explicit host authority for absolute paths and\\nowner-scoped Knowledge authority for `kb://` locators; they are not a general\\npermission engine or a remote MCP write grant. The candidate resolver SHALL admit\\nthe three native tools when the process has accepted native host authority or\\nhas a configured Knowledge root, and SHALL leave them unavailable when it has\\nneither.\",\n)\nt_reg = sub(\n    t_reg,\n    \"#### Scenario: Non-read-only tool is refused even when allowlisted\\n\",\n    \"#### Scenario: Native tools are admitted by Knowledge root alone\\n\\n- **WHEN** a process has a configured Knowledge root, no `tools.nativeExecutorId`, and allowlists `read`, `edit`, and `write`\\n- **THEN** the three tools are advertised and executable for `kb://` locators\\n- **AND** an absolute path fails closed with `executor_unavailable`\\n\\n#### Scenario: Non-read-only tool is refused even when allowlisted\\n\",\n)\n\nt_kn = block(tc, \"Code-owned Knowledge tools use the existing immutable read-only loop\")\nt_kn = sub(\n    t_kn,\n    \"The code-owned tool inventory SHALL include `knowledge_search` and `knowledge_read` in addition to `search_conversations`. Each SHALL declare `read_only`, require its own exact entry in `tools.allowed`, and participate\",\n    \"The code-owned tool inventory SHALL include `knowledge_search` in addition to `search_conversations`; Knowledge file access is the `kb://` locator of the native file tools. `knowledge_search` SHALL declare `read_only`, require its own exact entry in `tools.allowed`, and participate\",\n)\nt_kn = sub(\n    t_kn,\n    \"Changing either code-owned Knowledge declaration SHALL be a coordinated API/worker revision boundary because an accepted Run binds the exact declaration and a code-owned executor refuses drift. Before replacing binaries for the ranged-read declaration and again before replacing binaries for the passage-search declaration, the deployment SHALL quiesce\",\n    \"Changing the code-owned `knowledge_search` declaration SHALL be a coordinated API/worker revision boundary because an accepted Run binds the exact declaration and a code-owned executor refuses drift. Before replacing binaries for the passage-search declaration, the deployment SHALL quiesce\",\n)\nt_kn = sub(\n    t_kn,\n    \"- **WHEN** a deployment changes the code-owned declaration for either Knowledge tool\\n\",\n    \"- **WHEN** a deployment changes the code-owned `knowledge_search` declaration\\n\",\n)\nt_kn = sub(\n    t_kn,\n    \"- **WHEN** an operator allowlists either Knowledge tool\\n\",\n    \"- **WHEN** an operator allowlists `knowledge_search`\\n\",\n)\nt_kn = sub(\n    t_kn,\n    \"- **WHEN** a Run owner has no current Knowledge Spaces but the Knowledge tools are otherwise eligible\\n- **THEN** the tools are advertised as callable\\n\",\n    \"- **WHEN** a Run owner has no current Knowledge Spaces but `knowledge_search` is otherwise eligible\\n- **THEN** the tool is advertised as callable\\n\",\n)\nt_kn = sub(\n    t_kn,\n    \"#### Scenario: Incomplete Knowledge search stays incomplete after payload clearing\\n\",\n    \"#### Scenario: Removed reader fails closed for a bound Run\\n\\n- **WHEN** a Run accepted before removal has `knowledge_read` in its immutable tool snapshot and the model requests it\\n- **THEN** the call receives a recorded non-fatal unavailable refusal\\n- **AND** no shim, alias, or redirect to `read` is applied\\n\\n#### Scenario: Incomplete Knowledge search stays incomplete after payload clearing\\n\",\n)\n\nt_cr = block(tc, \"Conversation read uses the existing immutable read-only tool loop\")\nt_cr = sub(\n    t_cr,\n    \"in addition to `search_conversations`, `knowledge_search`, and `knowledge_read`.\",\n    \"in addition to `search_conversations` and `knowledge_search`.\",\n)\n\ntc_delta = f\"\"\"## MODIFIED Requirements\n\n{t_reg}\n{t_kn}\n{t_cr}\"\"\"\nwrite(\"tool-calling/spec.md\", tc_delta)\n",
